11.0.0 — a clip can be one to sixteen bars long, a first take is as long as you play, and the song loops as long as Arrange says

New since 10080, built by the Echoel Studio run; nothing here is device-verified yet. Each point
comes from a code walk of the task "make sixteen bars" on 10080.
- Note and drum editor, bottom bar: a length menu ("Length 1 Bar" and so on). "Repeat the Clip to"
  2, 4, 8 or 16 bars repeats what the clip holds, so a one-bar beat becomes sixteen bars of it;
  "Set the Length to" 1 to 16 bars sets the length outright (longer adds empty bars, shorter drops
  what starts past the end). A length that would run into the next clip on the track is dimmed,
  and the menu says why. One Undo.
- Recording: the first take on a song that plays nothing yet runs as long as you play. Before, a
  new song looped one bar, and everything played for sixteen bars landed in bar 1. Over a one-bar
  beat a take still plays into that bar, pass over pass, as before.
- Loop: the song loops to the end of its last clip, as Arrange counts its bars. Before, it looped
  to the last note, so a four-bar clip with notes only in bar 1 read "4 bars" and looped one.
- Four Tracks (the song a new install opens): the beat is in Scene 1 in Session too, so the plus
  under Drums no longer makes a second, empty clip. Arrange says "1 bar", not "1 bars".
- Learn: "Your First Track and Recording" names the length menu; "Comping and Loop Record" says
  what a one-bar loop does with each kind of take.
- Drum editor: the step grid is built column by column, only the columns on screen.
Limits, new: a sixteen-bar drum clip has 256 steps a row in the step grid, scrolled sideways.
Older limits as in 10080.

Previous: 10080. A green commit that changes this file uploads build 10000 + run number. A test
list, not a source for claims (ContentPipeline/CLAIMS.md).

One ask, as for 10080. Start a screen recording, open the app, and try to make sixteen bars in two
to five minutes: a beat, a bass line or a chord, then Play. No list and no protocol; stop wherever
it stops being possible or pleasant. The recording is the answer. What gets in the way in it is
the next work, in the order it happened.

The five checks of 10079 stay open and unchanged and rest until that recording exists.
